@lang en
IMPORT `tasco-vn19-ch4-claims`

-- Tests for Chapters IV to VI: the deadlines of Articles 12 and 16, the documents of Article 13,
-- Articles 14 and 17, and the regulative rules traced. Dates were counted by hand, month by month,
-- before the assertions were run; the counting is beside each.

§ `Tests, claims and disputes`

§§ `Article 12.1 and 12.2`

-- 120 days from 5 May 2026: 26 to 31 May, 56 to 30 Jun, 87 to 31 Jul, 118 to 31 Aug, 120 is 2 Sep.
#ASSERT `Article 12.1, the last day for written notice` (YMD 2026 5 5) 0 EQUALS YMD 2026 9 2
#ASSERT `Article 12.1, the last day for written notice` (YMD 2026 5 5) 10 EQUALS YMD 2026 9 12
-- One year from 1 May 2026 is 1 May 2027; a document sent that day is in time, the next day not.
#ASSERT `Article 12.2, the last day for the claim documents` (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 5 1
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 12.2, the claim has no validity` (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 (YMD 2027 5 1))
#ASSERT `Article 12.2, the claim has no validity` (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 (YMD 2027 5 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 12.2, the claim has no validity` (YMD 2026 5 1) 10 (YMD 2027 5 11))
-- An event on 29 Feb 2028: the year ends on 28 Feb 2029 (the calendar has no 29th; F23).
#ASSERT `Article 12.2, the last day for the claim documents` (YMD 2028 2 29) 0 EQUALS YMD 2029 2 28

§§ `Finding X18: the notice period can outlast the one-year bar`

-- An illness that began on 10 Jan 2026, death on 20 Nov 2026. Notice is due 120 days after the death:
-- 10 to 30 Nov, 41 to 31 Dec, 72 to 31 Jan, 100 to 28 Feb, 120 is 20 Mar 2027. The documents are
-- barred after 10 Jan 2027. A claimant who gives notice and sends documents on 1 Feb 2027, inside the
-- notice period, has a claim with no validity.
#ASSERT `Article 12.1, the last day for written notice` (YMD 2026 11 20) 0 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 20
#ASSERT `the notice period of 12.1 ends after the bar of 12.2` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 11 20)
#ASSERT `Article 12.2, the claim has no validity` (YMD 2026 1 10) 0 (YMD 2027 2 1)
-- Near miss: death on 1 Jun 2026; notice is due 29 Sep 2026, before the bar.
#ASSERT NOT (`the notice period of 12.1 ends after the bar of 12.2` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 6 1))
-- The edge is 245 days: an event on 1 Jan 2026 and discharge on day 245 (3 Sep) gives notice due on
-- 1 Jan 2027, the bar's own last day; discharge on day 246 (4 Sep) gives 2 Jan 2027, after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the notice period of 12.1 ends after the bar of 12.2` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 9 3))
#ASSERT `the notice period of 12.1 ends after the bar of 12.2` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 9 4)

§§ `Article 12.4 and 12.5`

#ASSERT `Article 12.4, the last day for payment` (YMD 2026 6 1) NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2026 6 16
#ASSERT `Article 12.4, the last day for payment` (YMD 2026 6 1) (JUST 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 11
#ASSERT `Article 12.5, the last day for written reasons for a refusal` (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 7 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 12.5, the last day for written reasons for a refusal` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE

-- Traced from the day complete documents arrive (clock 0, days). A refusal on day 25 discharges Tasco;
-- a payment on day 15 does; a payment on day 20 discharges neither branch, and both are breached at
-- day 31 (finding X19). Expected: FULFILLED, FULFILLED, BREACH.
#TRACE `Articles 12.4 and 12.5, Tasco's duty once the documents are complete` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `give written reasons for refusing the claim` AT 25

#TRACE `Articles 12.4 and 12.5, Tasco's duty once the documents are complete` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `pay the benefit` AT 15

#TRACE `Articles 12.4 and 12.5, Tasco's duty once the documents are complete` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco` DOES `pay the benefit` AT 20
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)

-- The claimant's notice, from discharge (clock 0): on day 120 in time; nothing by day 121, breach.
#TRACE `Article 12.1, the duty to give written notice, counted from discharge, end of treatment or death` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured or the beneficiary` DOES `give written notice of the insured event` AT 120

#TRACE `Article 12.1, the duty to give written notice, counted from discharge, end of treatment or death` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 121)

-- The documents, from the event of 10 Jan 2026 (clock 0): sent on day 387 (1 Feb 2027), after the
-- 365-day year: breach.
#TRACE `Article 12.2, the duty to send the claim documents, counted from the insured event` (YMD 2026 1 10) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured or the beneficiary` DOES `send the claim documents` AT 387

§§ `Article 13, the documents`

#ASSERT `Article 13, the documents for` (`with the contract` `the 10 million contract` `the illness stay claim`) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS LIST `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`, `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`, `13.3(a) medical records of the treatment`, `13.4(b) financial invoices or receipts`, `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`
#ASSERT `Article 13, the documents for` (`with the contract` `the special contract` `the illness stay claim`) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS LIST `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`, `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`, `13.3(a) medical records of the treatment`, `13.4(a) financial invoices for medical and related costs (original)`, `13.4(a) itemised statement of treatment costs`, `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`
-- A sum insured of exactly 20 million: 13.4 has no rule (finding X21).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 13, the documents for` `the illness stay claim` NOTHING FALSE
-- A death with no treatment needs no medical or payment documents, so the 20-million gap is not met.
#ASSERT `Article 13, the documents for` `the death claim` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS LIST `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`, `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`, `13.6(a) death certificate or extract, and proof of lawful inheritance`, `13.6(b) conclusion of a doctor or competent authority on the cause of death`, `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`
-- A traffic accident, the insured driving, with a police file, special contract.
#ASSERT `Article 13, the documents for` (`with the contract` `the special contract` (`with the circumstances` (LIST `the insured was driving a vehicle`) `the accident claim`)) (JUST `a traffic accident`) TRUE EQUALS LIST `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`, `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`, `13.3(a) medical records of the treatment`, `13.4(a) financial invoices for medical and related costs (original)`, `13.4(a) itemised statement of treatment costs`, `13.5(c) driving licence and vehicle registration`, `13.5(c) police preliminary report and investigation result or conclusion`, `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`
-- An accident in daily life, 10 million contract.
#ASSERT `Article 13, the documents for` (`with the contract` `the 10 million contract` `the accident claim`) (JUST `an accident in daily life`) FALSE EQUALS LIST `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`, `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`, `13.3(a) medical records of the treatment`, `13.4(b) financial invoices or receipts`, `13.5(a) accident report for an accident in daily life`, `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 13, the documents for` (`with the contract` `the 10 million contract` `the accident claim`) NOTHING FALSE
-- A partial permanent disability adds the injury assessment of 13.3(b).
#ASSERT `Article 13, the documents for` (`with the contract` `the 10 million contract` (`claiming` `II.2 partial permanent disability from accident` `an accident` (`with the injury` (JUST (`an injury` `partial permanent disability by loss` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 2) (JUST 30) 0 0)) `the accident claim`))) (JUST `an accident at work`) FALSE EQUALS LIST `13.1 claim form on Tasco's template (original)`, `13.2 contract or certificate, and list of insured persons (copy)`, `13.3(a) medical records of the treatment`, `13.3(b) injury certificate and the competent authority's injury assessment (original or notarised copy)`, `13.4(b) financial invoices or receipts`, `13.5(b) accident report for an accident at work`, `13.7 other documents Tasco requests`

§§ `Articles 14, 16 and 17`

#ASSERT `Article 14.1(c), Tasco may cancel the contract and refuse payment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 14.1(e), Tasco may refuse payment of` `the illness stay claim`)
#ASSERT `Article 14.1(e), Tasco may refuse payment of` (`outside Vietnam` `the illness stay claim`)
-- 90 days from 1 Jun 2026: 29 to 30 Jun, 60 to 31 Jul, 90 is 30 Aug. Three years from 1 Jun 2026.
#ASSERT `Article 16.1, the last day to complain about a claims decision` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 30
#ASSERT `Article 16.2, the last day to sue` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 1
#ASSERT `Article 17, the governing law` EQUALS "the law of Vietnam"
